"saransh2405","html_url":"https://github.com/saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229736,"global_rank":113227},{"name":"apc518/ffall","owner":"apc518","html_url":"https://github.com/apc518/ffall","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"apply an ffmpeg command to all files of a certain type in a directory","topics":[],"score":229730,"global_rank":113235},{"name":"baryhuang/metis-ai-services","owner":"baryhuang","html_url":"https://github.com/baryhuang/metis-ai-services","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229730,"global_rank":113236},{"name":"WittyAgnomen/political_bias","owner":"WittyAgnomen","html_url":"https://github.com/WittyAgnomen/political_bias","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"holds code for political bias paper","topics":[],"score":229726,"global_rank":113240},{"name":"ahoffer/circuit","owner":"ahoffer","html_url":"https://github.com/ahoffer/circuit","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229723,"global_rank":113249},{"name":"ktrnka/branded-image-gen-service","owner":"ktrnka","html_url":"https://github.com/ktrnka/branded-image-gen-service","s